      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most intellectually crushing argument is rooted in philosophical notions of desert and reciprocity. Your student needs to frame this as an attack on human dignity, asserting that society functions on a social contract where contribution earns reward; decoupling this creates a morally arbitrary system. They should argue that an unconditional handout undermines the intrinsic value of effort and competence, effectively rewarding idleness and eroding the shared commitment necessary for a functioning civil society. This reframes the debate from economics to ethics.",
      "source": "target",
